-- title:
--   Orders of j and j-1728 on X₀(N) without elliptic points
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and write $F$ for the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$: the subfield generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by all quotients $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms $f,g$ of equal weight on $\Gamma_0(N)$ (with $p_g\neq 0$). Let $y\in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), i.e. $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ with its integer coefficients mapped into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the $q$-expansion of $j$. Two implications are asserted, for places $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22) (a valuation subring of $F$, proper, containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and a principal ideal ring), with $P.\mathrm{ord}$ the associated normalised valuation. First: if $9\mid N$ or some prime $\ell\mid N$ satisfies $\ell\equiv 2\pmod 3$, then every $P$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(y)>0$ has $P.\mathrm{ord}(y)=3$. Second: if $4\mid N$ or some prime $\ell\mid N$ satisfies $\ell\equiv 3\pmod 4$, then every $P$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(y-1728)>0$ has $P.\mathrm{ord}(y-1728)=2$.
--
--   The hypotheses are exactly the classical conditions $\nu_3(N)=0$, respectively $\nu_2(N)=0$, under which $X_0(N)$ has no elliptic points of order $3$, respectively $2$; the conclusions record that the covering $X_0(N)\to X(1)$ is then totally ramified of degree $3$ over $j=0$ and of degree $2$ over $j=1728$, in the form of valuations of $y$ and $y-1728$ on the $q$-expansion function field. It is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ case from which the statement over an arbitrary algebraically closed field of characteristic zero, [`ModularCurve.ord_eq_three_and_ord_sub_eq_two_of_ord_pos_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_of_no_elliptic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_eq_three_and_ord_sub_eq_two_of_ord_pos_laurentBaseChange_gamma0_of_no_elliptic), is obtained by base change.
